  "estimatedMinutes": 1,
  "statement": "The measures of the interior angles of a convex polygon are in arithmetic progression. If the smallest angle is \\(100^\\circ\\) and the largest angle is \\(140^\\circ,\\) then the number of sides the polygon has is",
  "answerChoices": [
    {
      "label": "A",
      "text": "\\(6\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "B",
      "text": "\\(8\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "C",
      "text": "\\(10\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "D",
      "text": "\\(11\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "E",
      "text": "\\(12\\)"
    }
  ],
  "answer": {
    "letter": "a",
    "value": "6"
  },
  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1976-p14.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "The average angle is \\(\\frac{100+140}{2}=120^\\circ,\\) so the angle sum is \\(120n.\\) A convex \\(n\\)-gon has angle sum \\(180(n-2),\\) hence \\(120n=180(n-2)\\) and \\(n=6.\\)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is A.",
      "hints": [
        "The average of an arithmetic progression is the average of its first and last terms",
        "Equate \\(120n\\) with the interior-angle sum \\(180(n-2)\\)"
      ],
      "images": []
    }
  ],
